    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O`Farrell Cleere are delighted to bring to the market these exceptional four bedroom homes at Drumnigh Oaks, one of Portmarnock`s most exclusive and contemporary residential developments.\n\nOriginally developed by Ballymore, Drumnigh Oaks comprises just 30 carefully designed family homes, creating a small and private community in an outstanding coastal location. These homes offer an excellent combination of modern design, generous accommodation, energy efficiency and an enviable quality of life.\n\nEach of these homes extends to approximately 159 sq.m. (1,708 sq.ft.) and is arranged over three floors, providing exceptionally well proportioned accommodation throughout. The internal layouts are identical across the four homes, making this an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a modern, turnkey family home in one of North County Dublin`s most sough after locations.\n\nA particularly attractive feature of these homes is the south facing rear garden, providing an excellent private outdoor space with a sunny aspect throughout the day. The gardens are finished with a patio area and garden tap, while the homes are also wired for an electric vehicle charging point.\n\nInside, the accommodation has been designed with modern family living very much in mind. The contemporary kitchens feature bespoke internal cabinetry, while the bathrooms are finished to a high standard with contemporary sanitary ware and tiling. The three story layout provides excellent flexibility, with four bedrooms and generous living accommodation arranged over the three floors.\n\nEnergy efficiency is a major feature of Drumnigh Oaks. Ballymore designed the development with sustainability at its core, incorporating high quality insulation, advanced window systems, airtight construction, thermal bridge free design and sophisticated ventilation technology. The homes are designed to provide excellent thermal performance and a comfortable living environment while significantly reducing energy consumption.\n\nThe location is equally impressive. Portmarnock is renowned for its beautiful coastline and famous Velvet Strand, while the neighbouring village of Malahide provides an excellent selection of restaurants, cafés, bars, boutiques and amenities. The area is particularly well served by schools and sporting facilities, with the DART station providing convenient access towards Dublin City Centre. Dublin Airport and the M50 are also within easy reach.\n\nFor families, commuters and those looking for a more relaxed coastal lifestyle without sacrificing connectivity, Drumnigh Oaks represents a particularly attractive proposition.\n\nThese homes offer the opportunity to acquire a high quality Ballymore built home in a small, established development, with the added benefit of a south facing rear garden.\n"
      },
